     "wikidata": "Q1483375",
     "content": "A good knowledge of German is helpful in understanding some of the humor presented here.",
     "editions": 2,
     "unesco": false
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Museumkrems",
     "lat": 48.411329,
     "lng": 15.597168,
     "hours": "Apr-May Wed-Sun, holidays 11:00-18:00; Jun-Oct Daily 11:00-18:00; closed Nov-Mar",
     "price": "€5 (adults), €4 (concessions), free (children/youth under 19)",
     "wikidata": "Q1954788",
     "content": "Has well-curated permanent exhibits illustrating the history of Krems and the wider region, and hosts temporary exhibits of contemporary art.",
     "editions": 2,
     "unesco": false
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Gozzoburg",
     "lat": 48.411909,
     "lng": 15.602037,
     "hours": "",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q1540600",
     "content": "Built in the 13th century, this is one of the most significant medieval city buildings in Austria, and is now used for special exhibits. In 2006 and 2007 restoration work uncovered a remarkable set of 13th-century frescoes; along with the '",
     "editions": 4,
     "unesco": false
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Jewish Cemetery Krems",
     "lat": 48.417417,
     "lng": 15.623876,
     "hours": "",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q1716703",
     "content": "Established in 1880 for the Jewish community of Krems, the cemetery was abandoned in 1936 and now is a memorial under the auspices of Vienna Israelite Community. Located on the grounds is a 42m-long metal memorial by Hans Kupelwieser, engra",
     "editions": 2,
     "unesco": false
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Piaristenkirche",
     "lat": 48.412621,
     "lng": 15.599523,
     "hours": "",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q2091898",
     "content": "The oldest church in Krems. The earliest foundations date to the 13th century, while the current structure is from the late Gothic period of the early 16th century. The interior was remodeled during the Baroque era.",
     "editions": 4,
     "unesco": false
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Burgruine Rehberg",
     "lat": 48.43168,
     "lng": 15.5845,
     "hours": "Outer castle open 24 hrs, inner castle by prior arrangement only",
     "price": "Free",
     "wikidata": "Q19960786",
     "content": "Established in the 12th century, the castle changed hands many times over the centuries before it was finally abandoned in the early 19th century.",
     "editions": 2,
     "unesco": false
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "Burgruine Senftenberg",
     "lat": 48.4489,
     "lng": 15.5658,
     "hours": "",
     "price": "Free",
     "wikidata": "Q664922",
     "content": "The castle is located few kilometers north of Krems. Built in the 12th century, the fortress was abandoned after the Thirty Years' War. Easily accessible by foot and offers a great view of the surrounding vineyards.",
     "editions": 6,
     "unesco": false
    }
